@@ -18,6 +18,36 @@ Advanced reasoning adds durable tables for reasoning artifacts, artifact edges, r

 ## Loop

+### Super Reasoning Mode
+
+`super_reasoning.enabled = true` upgrades a port run from the five-stage
+starter plan into a long-horizon macro-plane. The reducer must produce a
+generic, target-derived plan with **9-12 stages**, not a baked target-specific
+checklist. The default runtime shape is:
+
+1. Contract capture
+2. Evidence map
+3. Reference harness
+4. Architecture skeleton
+5. Semantic surface
+6. Core execution
+7. Durability and state
+8. Integration fusion
+9. Parity expansion
+10. Performance closure
+11. Adversarial hardening, when requested
+12. Release signoff, when requested
+
+Each phase receives execution and signoff tasks. Signoff requires bounded write
+scope, reducer synthesis, verifier approval, Jankurai receipts, and parity/perf
+delta receipts. Independent phases may run in parallel only when the phase DAG
+has explicit dependency edges and the write scopes are disjoint.
+
+The active-memory contract is verifier-gated: episodic, semantic, procedural,
+and negative memory capsules are written only as structured summaries with
+source artifact hashes; raw private reasoning is not stored. Worker context is
+assembled from verified memory plus a bounded repository graph slice containing
+files, Rust symbols, call edges, tests, and parity cases relevant to the task.
+
+Parity closure follows a Redline-style evidence contract: generated manifest,
+approved case list, raw JSONL, summary JSON, gaps JSON, and hash-bound report
+inputs. Correctness, skipped required cases, missing performance data, and
+p95-over-budget regressions all spawn follow-up gap tasks until the gate passes.
+
 1. Capture the target request and repositories.
 2. Brainstorm candidate stages from target docs, source, tests, examples, and repo graph summaries.
 3. Finalize an ordered master plan with phases and task ownership.
diff --git a/docs/ZYAL/SUPER_REASONING.md b/docs/ZYAL/SUPER_REASONING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08c7d1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ZYAL/SUPER_REASONING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+# ZYAL Super Reasoning Contract
+
+This contract is for ambitious, multi-hour or multi-day ZYAL runs where a swarm
+of weaker agents must behave like one stronger reasoning system. It is generic:
+Redis parity, SQLite parity, a physics research effort, a protocol rewrite, and
+a large refactor all use the same runtime shape.
+
+## Design Goals
+
+- Force an explicit macro-plane before broad implementation work.
+- Split the macro-plane into phase tasks with dependency edges and bounded
+  write scopes.
+- Let independent phases run in parallel, but only through disjoint worktrees
+  and declared scopes.
+- Fuse work through reducer/verifier gates instead of accepting worker claims.
+- Compound knowledge through verified/rejected memory capsules.
+- Feed workers repository graph slices rather than unbounded context dumps.
+- Treat target-switched parity and performance evidence as first-class run
+  outputs.
+- Keep all raw private chain-of-thought out of durable storage.
+
+## Runtime Block
+
+```yaml
+super_reasoning:
+  enabled: true
+  macro_stage_target: 10
+  parallel_phases:
+    enabled: true
+    max_parallel_phases: 3
+    require_dependency_edges: true
+    disjoint_write_scopes_required: true
+  active_memory:
+    episodic: true
+    semantic: true
+    procedural: true
+    negative: true
+    max_context_tokens: 24000
+    write_requires:
+      - verified_or_rejected_status
+      - source_artifact_hash
+      - verifier_or_reducer_approval
+      - no_raw_chain_of_thought
+  graph:
+    store: sqlite
+    incremental: true
+    feed_workers: true
+    slice_node_budget: 256
+    include_tests: true
+    include_callers: true
+    include_callees: true
+  parity:
+    required_case_tags: [required, approved]
+    require_perf_data: true
+    prefer_ramdisk: true
+    default_p95_ms_max_ratio: 1.25
+  sandbox:
+    run_root: ".zyal/runs/${run.id}"
+    worktree_root: ".zyal/worktrees/${run.id}"
+    keep_between_ticks: true
+    gc_after: 14d
+    read_only_reference_repos: true
+  signoff:
+    require_reducer: true
+    require_verifier: true
+    require_jankurai: true
+    require_parity_delta: true
+    max_unresolved_objections: 0
+```
+
+## Macro Plane
+
+The default macro plane is 10 stages; the runtime clamps requested stage count
+to 9-12.
+
+| Stage | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| Contract capture | Freeze objective, acceptance criteria, non-goals, source-use rules, and risk budget. |
+| Evidence map | Index docs, source, tests, examples, benchmark artifacts, and known gaps. |
+| Reference harness | Build target-switched harnesses and approved manifests before implementation claims. |
+| Architecture skeleton | Establish candidate architecture, modules, adapters, and build/test scaffolding. |
+| Semantic surface | Implement APIs/protocols under parity tests. |
+| Core execution | Implement the core algorithms/data flow with bounded scopes. |
+| Durability and state | Add persistence/recovery/state-machine behavior when relevant. |
+| Integration fusion | Merge worker branches and heal cross-phase regressions. |
+| Parity expansion | Expand coverage and spawn gap tasks from failures/skips/missing cases. |
+| Performance closure | Measure and close reference/candidate perf gaps. |
+| Adversarial hardening | Optional red-team/fuzz/chaos/security/resource passes. |
+| Release signoff | Optional final evidence bundle and acceptance packet. |
+
+## Worker Contract
+
+Every worker assignment must include:
+
+- task id, phase id, and stage objective;
+- declared write scope;
+- bounded graph slice;
+- bounded verified memory pack;
+- proof lane;
+- forbidden raw-reasoning persistence;
+- stop rules for scope drift, proof failure, Jankurai regression, and repeated
+  quarantine.
+
+## Memory Contract
+
+Memory writes are not free-form notes. A permanent memory capsule must have:
+
+- `verified` or `rejected` status;
+- source artifact id/hash;
+- evidence level of external-grounding or stronger;
+- reducer/verifier approval;
+- no raw private chain-of-thought;
+- negative/falsifying evidence when it records a rejected approach.
+
+The memory system should store four families:
+
+- episodic: what happened in the run;
+- semantic: stable target/candidate behavior facts;
+- procedural: reusable tested procedures;
+- negative: dead ends, false hypotheses, perf traps, flaky harnesses.
+
+## Graph Contract
+
+The graph starts with the existing SQLite-backed repo graph and should grow
+toward an incremental code-intelligence graph:
+
+- nodes: files, docs, tests, modules, functions, structs, enums, impls, methods,
+  commands, phases, tasks, parity cases, perf budgets, memory capsules;
+- edges: contains, imports, calls, tests, implements, derives_from,
+  parity_covers, phase_owns, changed_by, supports, critiques, reduces;
+- worker queries: by task write scope, touched function, failing parity case,
+  failing test, phase id, or memory claim.
+
+## Parity Contract
+
+Parity is target-switched: the same case runs against reference and candidate
+adapters. Required or approved cases fail the gate when missing, skipped, failed,
+or missing required performance data. Reports should produce:
+
+```text
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/generated_manifest.json
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/approved-ci.txt
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/raw.jsonl
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/summary.json
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/gaps.json
+```
+
+For speed, parity runners should support tmpfs/RAM-disk execution and in-memory
+reference/candidate configuration when the target allows it.
+
+## Completion Rule
+
+A super-reasoning run may not finish with:
+
+- model-only claims;
+- missing required parity cases;
+- skipped required parity cases;
+- unchecked performance budgets;
+- unmerged verified worker branches;
+- unresolved critical objections;
+- dirty primary worktree;
+- raw reasoning stored as memory;
+- copied reference implementation text.
